markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Section 5: Classification, Start to Finish</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 8-9</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach two curriculum lessons, the classification half of the unit's build-and-test arc, mirroring Section 4's regression arc. Students build a nearest-neighbors classifier by hand, then in code, before learning that "how good is this model?" has no single answer, it depends on which kind of mistake costs more.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 8:</b> Building Classifiers</div>
  <a href="PASTE_UNIT_2_LESSON_8_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 8</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 9:</b> Testing Classifiers</div>
  <a href="PASTE_UNIT_2_LESSON_9_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 9</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Learn the nearest-neighbors algorithm: to label something new, look at the most similar examples you've already seen</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get ahead of a real misconception: more neighbors isn't always better</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Compare two classifiers using accuracy, recall, and precision, and see why the "more accurate" model isn't automatically the better one</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; Tune a confidence threshold yourself and watch recall and precision trade off against each other</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> both lessons use a deliberately higher-stakes framing than Section 4 did, late mail is an inconvenience, a toxic berry is a real safety risk. That shift in stakes is what makes the precision/recall trade-off actually matter, not just a formula to memorize.</div>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 700px;">
